Error [E0202]: Cannot write to `item` — it does not have the write-access marker `&`; required before calling `.touch()`
  --> multi_trait_receiver_access_follows_first_match_dispatch_order_2.jet:11:27
    |
 11 |         call(() -> { item.touch() })
    |                           ^^^^^
 Why: This method edits the value it's called on; the write-access marker `&` is required
 Fix: Declare `item := ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0202

Error [E0224]: This call writes `item`, but `item` has no `&` mark
  --> multi_trait_receiver_access_follows_first_match_dispatch_order_2.jet:11:22
    |
 11 |         call(() -> { item.touch() })
    |                      ^^^^
 Why: The method is declared with `&self`, so the call writes the named place it is called on; the mark sits on that place, the same way `edit(&buf)` and `consume(^text)` mark arguments
 Fix: Write `&item`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0224

